	lifecycle_state = <"published">
	other_contributors = <"Vebjørn Arntzen, Oslo University Hospital, Norway (openEHR Editor)","Silje Ljosland Bakke, Helse Vest IKT AS, Norway (openEHR Editor)","SB Bhattacharyya, Bhattacharyyas Clinical Records Research & Informatics LLP, India","Hugo Claudio Briceño García, Catsalut, Spain","Clara Calleja Vega, CatSalut. Servei Català de la Salut., Spain","Christian Chevalley, ADOC, Thailand","Giovanni Delussu, crs4, Italy","Mona Didriksen, Helse Vest IKT, Norway","Manuela Domingo, hospital general universitario dr. balmis, Spain","Gunn Elin Blakkisrud, DIPS ASA, Norway","Aleksander Furnes, Helse Nord IKT, Norway","Ciprian Gerstenberger, HN IKT, Norway","Rosane Gotardo, Systema Ltda., Brazil","Heather Grain, Llewelyn Grain Informatics, Australia","Atle Hansen, Universitetssykehuset Nord-Norge, Norway","Evelyn Hovenga, EJSH Consulting, Australia","Susanna Jönsson, Region Värmland, Sweden","Mika Kiviaho, Tietoevry Care, Finland","June Marie Nepstad Knappskog, Helse Nord IKT AS, Norway (openEHR Editor), Norway","Martin Koch, Servei Català de la Salut, Spain","Ronald Krawec, Alberta Health Services, Canada","Lise Kristin Knutsen, Oslo universitetssykehus, Norway","Anjali Kulkarni, Karkinos, India","Kanika Kuwelker, Helse Vest IKT, Norway","Jörgen Kuylenstierna, eWeave AB, Sweden","Eli Larsen, UNN, Norway","Liv Laugen, ​Oslo University Hospital, Norway, Norway (openEHR Editor)","Darin Leonhardt, PLRI für medizinische Informatik/ Medizinische Hochschule, Germany","Heather Leslie, Atomica Informatics, Australia (openEHR Editor)","Ruth Lochan, Akademiska Sjukhuset Uppsala, Sweden","Michael Lutz, BITsoft, Germany","Hanne Marte Bårholm, Helse Vest IKT, Norway (openEHR Norway redaktør)","Ian McNicoll, freshEHR Clinical Informatics, United Kingdom","Arunakiry Natarajan, medondo, Germany","Svenne Naumann, Finnmarkssykehuset, Norway","Olha Nikolaieva, University Hospital Basel, Switzerland","Terje Nordberg, Helse Bergen, Norway","Mikael Nyström, Cambio Healthcare Systems AB, Sweden","Marlene Pérez Colman, Digital Health and Care Wales, United Kingdom","Benjamin Senst, Germany","Andre Smitt-Ingebretsen, Sørlandet sykehus HF, Norway","Norwegian Review Summary, Norwegian Public Hospitals, Norway","John Tore Valand, Helse Vest IKT, Norway (openEHR Editor)","Wouter Zanen, Eurotranplant, Netherlands">
	details = <
		["de"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::de]>
			purpose = <"Für die Erstellung eines Rahmens für die Aufzeichnung von Antworten auf vordefinierte Screening-Fragen zu gesundheitlichen Problemen bei genetischen und nicht-genetischen Familienmitgliedern.">
			keywords = <"Familie, Geschichte, Gesundheit, Zustand, Problem, Diagnose, Familiengeschichte, relativ, biologisch, Beziehung, Hintergrund, genetisch", ...>
			use = <"*Use to create a framework for recording answers to pre-defined screening questions about health-related problems found in both genetic and non-genetic family members.

Traditionally the scope of family history has been focused on identifying factors or biomarkers in genetically related family members. Non-genetic family members may also be included, such as adopted or long term fostered children, those related by marriage, or other unrelated individuals who participate in the regular life and influence of the family.

The intended scope of this archetype is to include the broadest range of problems or issues that might be found within families. It includes problems or diagnoses that are:
- genetically inheritable, such as breast cancer or Huntington’s disease
- not genetically inheritable but influenced by psychological, social, or environmental factors related to the family, such as exposure to toxins in the family home, domestic violence, sexual abuse, alcoholism and other addictions.

This archetype has two discrete approaches for screening for family history:
- All relationships - Does  *anyone* in the family have ‘Problem/diagnosis name’? 
- Specified relationship - Does your 'Relationship'  have ‘Problem/diagnosis name’? 

Common use cases include, but are not limited to:
- Systematic questioning in any consultation, for example:
--- Is there a history of heart disease in the family?
--- Is there a history of mental health problems in the family?
--- Is there a history of addiction in the family?
--- Did your mother have diabetes?
- Specific questioning related to chronic disease management or preventive health.

Templates for specific use cases may be constrained to relationships with genetic family members if required.

The semantics of this archetype are intentionally loose, and querying this archetype would normally only be useful or safe within the context of each specific template. In a template, each data element would usually be renamed to the specific question asked. Where value sets have been proposed for common use cases, these can be adapted for local use by using the DV_TEXT or the DV_BOOLEAN datatypes choice to match each specific use case.

Use separate EVENTs to specify whether the questions relate to a point in time or an interval of time. For example: \"Do any family members have COVID now?\" as a point in time EVENT and \"Have any family members had COVID during the past 4 weeks?\" as an interval EVENT.

The source of the information in a questionnaire response may vary in different contexts but can be specifically identified using the 'Information provider' element in the Reference Model.

This archetype has been designed to be used as a screening tool or to record simple questionnaire-format data for use in situations such as a disease registry. If the screening questionnaire identifies the presence of a health concern in a family member, it is recommended that the clinical system record the specific details using the EVALUATION.family_history archetype or the CLUSTER.family_prevalence archetype. (en)">
			misuse = <"*Not to be used to record details about the presence or absence of a family-related problem outside of a screening context. Use EVALUATION.family_history or EVALUATION.exclusion_specific for these purposes.

Not to be used to record details about a specific health-related problem. Use EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis for this purpose.

Not to be used to record a Family Pedigree chart of health problems/diagnoses. Use the EVALUATION.family_history archetype for this purpose. (en)">
		>
		["nb"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
			purpose = <"For å lage et rammeverk for registrering av svar på forhåndsdefinerte spørsmål om helserelaterte forhold hos både genetiske og ikke-genetiske familiemedlemmer.">
			keywords = <"familie, historie, anamnese, helse, forhold, problem, diagnose, familiehistorie, slektning, biologisk, bakgrunn, genetisk", ...>
			use = <"Brukes for å lage et rammeverk for registrering av svar på forhåndsdefinerte spørsmål om helserelaterte forhold hos både genetiske og ikke-genetiske familiemedlemmer.

Tradisjonelt har omfanget av en familieanamnese vært fokusert på å identifisere faktorer eller biomarkører hos genetisk beslektede familiemedlemmer. Denne arketypen utvider omfanget til også å kunne inkludere ikke-genetiske familiemedlemmer, for eksempel adopterte barn, fosterbarn, ektefeller, eller andre ubeslektede individer som inngår i familiens daglige liv og påvirkning.

Arketypen omfatter et bredest mulig spekter av problemer, bekymringer eller plager som kan oppstå i familier. Dette omfatter kjente problemer eller diagnoser som:
- Genetisk arvelige, for eksempel brystkreft eller Huntingtons sykdom.
- Ikke-genetisk arvelige, men som likevel kan være påvirket av psykologiske, sosiale eller miljømessige faktorer knyttet til familien, for eksempel eksponering for giftstoffer i hjemmet, vold i hjemmet, seksuelle overgrep, alkoholisme eller andre avhengigheter.

Denne arketypen har to tilnærminger for å kartlegge familieanamnese:
- Alle relasjoner – Har et hvilket som helst familiemedlem «Problem-/diagnosenavn»?
- Spesifikk relasjon – Har det spesifikke familiemedlemmet, som er angitt under \"Relasjon\" \"Problem-/diagnosenavn\"?

Vanlige bruksområder inkluderer, men er ikke begrenset til:
- Systematiske spørsmål ved konsultasjoner, for eksempel:
--- Er det kjent hjertesykdom i familien?
--- Er det psykiske helseproblemer i familien?
--- Finnes det avhengighetsproblemer i familien?
--- Har din mor diabetes?
- Spesifikke spørsmål relatert til håndtering av kronisk sykdom eller forebyggende helse.

Templater for spesifikke brukstilfeller kan, om nødvendig, begrenses til relasjoner med genetiske familiemedlemmer.

Semantikken til denne arketypen er med vilje løst definert, og spørringer etter data i denne arketypen vil normalt bare være hensiktsmessig eller sikker i konteksten av det spesifikke templatet. I et templat vil hvert dataelement vanligvis døpes om til det spesifikke spørsmålet man ønsker svar på. Flere steder er det foreslått verdisett som passer til de vanligste bruksområder, men det er allikevel mulig å tilpasse/endre verdisett for lokal bruk ved å benytte de alternative datatypene DV_TEXT eller DV_BOOLEAN for å harmonere verdisettet til hvert enkelt brukstilfelle.

Bruk egne EVENTer for å skille mellom spørsmål som omhandler et hvilket som helst tidspunkt eller et tidsintervall. For eksempel; \"Har noen familiemedlemmer COVID nå?\" som en tidspunktshendelse (point in time EVENT) sammenlignet med \"Har noen familiemedlemmer hatt COVID de siste fire ukene?\" som en intervallhendelse (Interval EVENT)

Kilden til informasjonen i et spørreskjema kan variere i ulike kontekster, men kan identifiseres spesifikt ved å benytte \"Information provider\"-elementet i openEHR referansemodellen.

Denne arketypen er laget for å bli brukt i et spørreskjema eller for å registrere enkle strukturerte data til for eksempel et sykdomsregister. Dersom det i spørreskjemaet identifiseres at signifikante helserelaterte forhold er tilstede hos et familiemedlem, anbefales det at disse registreres og lagres i pasientjournalen i en relevant arketype, for eksempel i arketypene EVALUATION.family_history (Familieanamnese) eller i CLUSTER.family_prevalence (Familieprevalens).">
			misuse = <"Brukes ikke for å registrere tilstedeværelse eller fravær av helserelaterte forhold hos familiemedlemmer utenfor konteksten av kartleggingen. Bruk arketypene EVALUATION.family_history (Familieanamnese) eller EVALUATION.exclusion_specific (Eksklusjonsutsagn - spesifikt) for dette formålet.

Brukes ikke som basis for et slektstre over helseproblemer og diagnoser. Bruk arketypen EVALUATION.family_history (Familieanamnese) for dette formålet.">
		>
		["en"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::en]>
			purpose = <"To create a framework for recording answers to pre-defined screening questions about health-related problems found in both genetic and non-genetic family members.">
			keywords = <"family","history","health","condition","problem","diagnosis","family","history","relative","biological","relationship","background","genetic">
			copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
			use = <"Use to create a framework for recording answers to pre-defined screening questions about health-related problems found in both genetic and non-genetic family members.

Traditionally the scope of family history has been focused on identifying factors or biomarkers in genetically related family members. Non-genetic family members may also be included, such as adopted or long term fostered children, those related by marriage, or other unrelated individuals who participate in the regular life and influence of the family.

The intended scope of this archetype is to include the broadest range of problems or issues that might be found within families. It includes problems or diagnoses that are:
- genetically inheritable, such as breast cancer or Huntington’s disease
- not genetically inheritable but influenced by psychological, social, or environmental factors related to the family, such as exposure to toxins in the family home, domestic violence, sexual abuse, alcoholism and other addictions.

This archetype has two discrete approaches for screening for family history:
- All relationships - Does *anyone* in the family have ‘Problem/diagnosis name’? 
- Specified relationship - Does your 'Relationship' have ‘Problem/diagnosis name’? 

Common use cases include, but are not limited to:
- Systematic questioning in any consultation, for example:
--- Is there a history of heart disease in the family?
--- Is there a history of mental health problems in the family?
--- Is there a history of addiction in the family?
--- Did your mother have diabetes?
- Specific questioning related to chronic disease management or preventive health.

Templates for specific use cases may be constrained to relationships with genetic family members if required.

The semantics of this archetype are intentionally loose, and querying this archetype would normally only be useful or safe within the context of each specific template. In a template, each data element would usually be renamed to the specific question asked. Where value sets have been proposed for common use cases, these can be adapted for local use by using the DV_TEXT or the DV_BOOLEAN datatypes choice to match each specific use case.

Use separate EVENTs to specify whether the questions relate to a point in time or an interval of time. For example: \"Do any family members have COVID now?\" as a point in time EVENT and \"Have any family members had COVID during the past 4 weeks?\" as an interval EVENT.

The source of the information in a questionnaire response may vary in different contexts but can be specifically identified using the 'Information provider' element in the Reference Model.

This archetype has been designed to be used as a screening tool or to record simple questionnaire-format data for use in situations such as a disease registry. If the screening questionnaire identifies the presence of a health concern in a family member, it is recommended that the clinical system record the specific details using the EVALUATION.family_history archetype or the CLUSTER.family_prevalence archetype.">
			misuse = <"Not to be used to record details about the presence or absence of a family-related problem outside of a screening context. Use EVALUATION.family_history or EVALUATION.exclusion_specific for these purposes.

Not to be used to record a Family Pedigree chart of health problems/diagnoses. Use the EVALUATION.family_history archetype for this purpose.">
		>
		["ca"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::ca]>
			purpose = <"Crear un marc per registrar respostes a preguntes de cribratge predefinides sobre problemes relacionats amb la salut trobats tant en familiars genètics com no genètics.">
			keywords = <"família","antecedents","salut","condició","problema","diagnòstic","antecedents","familiars","familiar","biològic","relació","entorn","genètic">
			copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
			use = <"S'utilitza per crear un marc per registrar respostes a preguntes de cribratge predefinides sobre problemes relacionats amb la salut trobats tant en familiars genètics com no genètics.

Tradicionalment, l'abast dels antecedents familiars s'ha centrat a identificar factors o biomarcadors en familiars amb relació genètica. També es poden incloure familiars sense relació genètica, com ara fills adoptats o acollits a llarg termini, persones emparentades per matrimoni o altres individus sense parentiu que participen en la vida habitual i la influència de la família.

L'abast previst d'aquest arquetip és incloure el ventall més ampli possible de problemes o qüestions que es puguin trobar dins les famílies. Inclou problemes o diagnòstics que són:
- heretables genèticament, com el càncer de mama o la malaltia de Huntington
- no heretables genèticament però influïts per factors psicològics, socials o ambientals relacionats amb la família, com l'exposició a tòxics a la llar familiar, la violència domèstica, l'abús sexual, l'alcoholisme i altres addiccions.

Aquest arquetip té dos enfocaments diferenciats per fer el cribratge dels antecedents familiars:
- Totes les relacions - Té *algú* de la família el «Nom del problema/diagnòstic»?
- Relació especificada - Té la teva «Relació» el «Nom del problema/diagnòstic»?

Els casos d'ús habituals inclouen, entre d'altres:
- Preguntes sistemàtiques en qualsevol consulta, per exemple:
--- Hi ha antecedents de malaltia cardíaca a la família?
--- Hi ha antecedents de problemes de salut mental a la família?
--- Hi ha antecedents d'addicció a la família?
--- La teva mare tenia diabetis?
- Preguntes específiques relacionades amb el maneig de malalties cròniques o la salut preventiva.

Les plantilles per a casos d'ús específics es poden restringir, si cal, a relacions amb familiars genètics.

La semàntica d'aquest arquetip és intencionadament laxa, i consultar aquest arquetip normalment només serà útil o segur dins del context de cada plantilla específica. En una plantilla, cada element de dades normalment es reanomena amb la pregunta concreta formulada. Quan s'han proposat conjunts de valors per a casos d'ús habituals, aquests es poden adaptar per a l'ús local mitjançant l'elecció del tipus de dada DV_TEXT o DV_BOOLEAN segons el cas d'ús concret.

Utilitza EVENTs separats per especificar si les preguntes fan referència a un moment puntual o a un interval de temps. Per exemple: «Algun familiar té la COVID ara?» com a EVENT puntual i «Algun familiar ha tingut la COVID durant les últimes 4 setmanes?» com a EVENT d'interval.

La font de la informació d'una resposta al qüestionari pot variar segons el context, però es pot identificar específicament mitjançant l'element «Proveïdor de la informació» del model de referència.

Aquest arquetip s'ha dissenyat per utilitzar-se com a eina de cribratge o per registrar dades senzilles en format de qüestionari, per a situacions com ara un registre de malalties. Si el qüestionari de cribratge identifica la presència d'un problema de salut en un familiar, es recomana que el sistema clínic registri els detalls específics utilitzant l'arquetip EVALUATION.family_history o l'arquetip CLUSTER.family_prevalence.">
			misuse = <"No s'ha d'utilitzar per registrar detalls sobre la presència o absència d'un problema familiar fora d'un context de cribratge. Utilitza EVALUATION.family_history o EVALUATION.exclusion_specific per a aquestes finalitats.

No s'ha d'utilitzar per registrar un arbre genealògic (pedigrí familiar) de problemes/diagnòstics de salut. Utilitza l'arquetip EVALUATION.family_history per a aquesta finalitat.">
		>
		["es"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::es]>
			purpose = <"Crear un marco para registrar respuestas a preguntas de cribado predefinidas sobre problemas relacionados con la salud encontrados tanto en familiares genéticos como no genéticos.">
			keywords = <"familia","antecedentes","salud","condición","problema","diagnóstico","antecedentes","familiares","familiar","biológico","relación","entorno","genético">
			copyright = <"© openEHR Foundation">
			use = <"Se utiliza para crear un marco para registrar respuestas a preguntas de cribado predefinidas sobre problemas relacionados con la salud encontrados tanto en familiares genéticos como no genéticos.

Tradicionalmente, el alcance de los antecedentes familiares se ha centrado en identificar factores o biomarcadores en familiares con relación genética. También pueden incluirse familiares sin relación genética, como hijos adoptados o acogidos a largo plazo, personas emparentadas por matrimonio u otros individuos sin parentesco que participan en la vida habitual y la influencia de la familia.

El alcance previsto de este arquetipo es incluir el abanico más amplio posible de problemas o cuestiones que puedan encontrarse dentro de las familias. Incluye problemas o diagnósticos que son:
- heredables genéticamente, como el cáncer de mama o la enfermedad de Huntington
- no heredables genéticamente pero influidos por factores psicológicos, sociales o ambientales relacionados con la familia, como la exposición a tóxicos en el hogar familiar, la violencia doméstica, el abuso sexual, el alcoholismo y otras adicciones.

Este arquetipo tiene dos enfoques diferenciados para el cribado de los antecedentes familiares:
- Todas las relaciones - ¿Tiene *alguien* de la familia el «Nombre del problema/diagnóstico»?
- Relación especificada - ¿Tiene tu «Relación» el «Nombre del problema/diagnóstico»?

Los casos de uso habituales incluyen, entre otros:
- Preguntas sistemáticas en cualquier consulta, por ejemplo:
--- ¿Hay antecedentes de enfermedad cardíaca en la familia?
--- ¿Hay antecedentes de problemas de salud mental en la familia?
--- ¿Hay antecedentes de adicción en la familia?
--- ¿Tu madre tenía diabetes?
- Preguntas específicas relacionadas con el manejo de enfermedades crónicas o la salud preventiva.

Las plantillas para casos de uso específicos pueden restringirse, si es necesario, a relaciones con familiares genéticos.

La semántica de este arquetipo es intencionadamente laxa, y consultar este arquetipo normalmente solo será útil o seguro dentro del contexto de cada plantilla específica. En una plantilla, cada elemento de datos normalmente se renombra con la pregunta concreta formulada. Cuando se han propuesto conjuntos de valores para casos de uso habituales, estos pueden adaptarse para el uso local mediante la elección del tipo de dato DV_TEXT o DV_BOOLEAN según el caso de uso concreto.

Utiliza EVENTs separados para especificar si las preguntas hacen referencia a un momento puntual o a un intervalo de tiempo. Por ejemplo: «¿Algún familiar tiene COVID ahora?» como EVENT puntual y «¿Algún familiar ha tenido COVID durante las últimas 4 semanas?» como EVENT de intervalo.

La fuente de la información de una respuesta al cuestionario puede variar según el contexto, pero puede identificarse específicamente mediante el elemento «Proveedor de la información» del modelo de referencia.

Este arquetipo se ha diseñado para utilizarse como herramienta de cribado o para registrar datos sencillos en formato de cuestionario, para situaciones como un registro de enfermedades. Si el cuestionario de cribado identifica la presencia de un problema de salud en un familiar, se recomienda que el sistema clínico registre los detalles específicos utilizando el arquetipo EVALUATION.family_history o el arquetipo CLUSTER.family_prevalence.">
			misuse = <"No debe utilizarse para registrar detalles sobre la presencia o ausencia de un problema familiar fuera de un contexto de cribado. Utiliza EVALUATION.family_history o EVALUATION.exclusion_specific para estos fines.

No debe utilizarse para registrar un árbol genealógico (pedigrí familiar) de problemas/diagnósticos de salud. Utiliza el arquetipo EVALUATION.family_history para esta finalidad.">
		>
	>
	other_details = <
